Analyze bug {{.key}}: "{{.title}}". Severity: {{.severity}}.

READ:
(1) Bug report at {{.file_path}} — reproduction steps, expected vs actual behavior, environment
(2) Codebase: trace the code path involved. Use debugging skill to follow the failure.

DETERMINE:
- Root cause (exact code location causing the failure)
- Component type: FRONTEND (UI visible, user interaction) or BACKEND (API, data, server-side)
- Whether severity needs adjustment
- Whether any linked entity should be set: shark bug update {{.key}} --link={entity_key}

DOCUMENT findings:
shark bug note {{.key}} 'ANALYSIS: component={frontend|backend}, root_cause={description}, files={file1,file2}, severity_confirmed={yes|adjusted to X}'

ROUTE:
- Root cause identified → shark status advance {{.key}}
- Not reproducible / expected behavior → shark bug note {{.key}} 'WONT_FIX: {reason}' then shark status set {{.key}} wont_fix
- Is a duplicate → shark bug note {{.key}} 'DUPLICATE of {other_key}' then shark status set {{.key}} duplicate
